  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 154c50ec217d4454588993d74be1192b, type: 3}
  m_Name: MenuTips
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TipsData
  tips:
  - A downed teammate can't be hit, but they are bleeding out. <b><color=#FD3971>Hold
    interact</color></b> next to them to revive - the timer pauses while you do.
  - Downed for too long means <b><color=#FD3971>KO</color></b>. A KO'd Raider can't be revived
    - they return once the team clears the area.
  - Your <b><color=#FD3971>accessory</color></b> blocks one hit, then pops off. Walk over
    and pick it up to wear it again.
  - While you have <b><color=#FD3971>Shield</color></b>, hits eat the Shield first and your
    accessory stays on. Shield is earned in battle - it never recharges on its own.
  - During a Break you can pay <b><color=#FD3971>Coins</color></b> to repair a damaged accessory.
    The more damaged it is, the higher the price.
  - '<b><color=#FD3971>Breathing Breaks</color></b> are your safe moment: heal at the Shrine,
    shop at the Store, upgrade at the Blacksmith.'
  - Once the area is secured, the team can <b><color=#FD3971>vote to skip</color></b> the
    rest of the Break.
  - You can't afford everything at the Store and Blacksmith. The <b><color=#FD3971>Blacksmith</color></b>
    adds a perk to the weapon you are holding - choose wisely.
  - 'Mix elements for <b><color=#FD3971>reactions</color></b>: Fire + Ice is Thermal Shock,
    Fire + Lightning is Overload, Ice + Lightning is Shatter.'
  - <b><color=#FD3971>Burn</color></b> stacks for damage, <b><color=#FD3971>Chill</color></b> slows
    more with every hit until the enemy freezes, and <b><color=#FD3971>Shock</color></b>
    sets up a stun on the next electric hit.
  - A <b><color=#FD3971>Cursed Rift</color></b> offers a Rift Mutation, but you pay a price
    for it. Read the card before you take it.
  - <b><color=#FD3971>Rift Mutations</color></b> are rare, can't be stacked, and bend your
    whole run. Pick the ones that fit your build.
  - 'Level-ups pause the action: pick one of three cards. Don''t like them? Spend
    a <b><color=#FD3971>Reroll</color></b> if you have one.'
  - Some <b><color=#FD3971>Elites</color></b> carry a chest. Take them down - or chase them
    - to claim it.
  - 'Hold <b><color=#FD3971>Tab</color></b> (Select on a gamepad) to see everything you
    are running: skill, passive, perks and upgrades.'
  - Press <b><color=#FD3971>M</color></b> (R2 on a gamepad) to open the full minimap and
    plan your next move.
  - '<b><color=#FD3971>Team Challenges</color></b> are optional: every Raider must Ready
    up inside the area. Win and the whole team earns a Rift Mutation.'
  - A <b><color=#FD3971>Traversal Challenge</color></b> needs the whole team to cross the
    gaps before the timer runs out. Don't leave anyone behind.
  - More Raiders means tougher enemies and more XP per level. <b><color=#FD3971>Cover
    each other</color></b> - the game scales with your squad.
  - '<b><color=#FD3971>Dash</color></b> is an escape button: use it to slip out of a swarm.
    It gets its own upgrades as you level.'
  - 'Every hero grows through <b><color=#FD3971>Ascensions</color></b>: one line for a weapon
    weight, one for an element. Rank 3 unlocks a special effect.'
  - Hero upgrades have <b><color=#FD3971>3 ranks</color></b>. Rank 3 usually unlocks something
    special - worth sticking with.
  - 'Weapons come in six families: Pistol, SMG, Assault Rifle, Shotgun, Sniper and
    Grenade Launcher. See them all in the <b><color=#FD3971>Loadout</color></b> tab.'
  - 'Every weapon has a <b><color=#FD3971>Weight</color></b>: Light, Medium or Heavy. Light
    weapons make you move faster, Heavy ones slow you down.'
  - Heavy weapons hit hard but slow you down. <b><color=#FD3971>Brute</color></b> and <b><color=#FD3971>Yoru</color></b>
    lose the slowdown at Heavy Mastery rank 3.
